You are given three tables: Students, Friends and Packages. 
Students contains two columns: ID and Name. 
Friends contains two columns: ID and Friend_ID (ID of the ONLY best friend). 
Packages contains two columns: ID and Salary (offered salary in $ thousands per month).

Write a query to output the names of those students whose best friends got offered a higher salary than them. 
Names must be ordered by the salary amount offered to the best friends. 
It is guaranteed that no two students got same salary offer.


SOLUTION: 

SELECT Students.Name

FROM Packages a
JOIN Students ON Students.ID = a.ID -- sorts out salary and name for the original student
JOIN Friends ON Friends.ID = a.ID -- joins the friend
JOIN Packages b ON Friends.Friend_ID = b.ID -- sorts out salary for the friend

WHERE b.Salary > a.Salary -- performs the required salary check
ORDER BY b.Salary -- orders by the offer size of friend
